The wider pass exposed only lint/style findings, not behavioral failures. During self-review I found one concurrency edge worth tightening: lock-order tracking was thread-local, so a second thread in the same process could attempt a new project lock while another thread held the home lock. I’m closing that process-wide ordering gap and adding a regression before rerunning the gates.
